Pindrop runs third-party security scanners as external subprocesses. Those tools
are separately licensed and are neither distributed with, nor linked into, this
software:

  - Trivy (Apache-2.0)          https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy
  - OSV-Scanner (Apache-2.0)    https://github.com/google/osv-scanner
  - Opengrep (LGPL-2.1)         https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep
  - TruffleHog (AGPL-3.0)       https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog

`pindrop setup` downloads these binaries for the user's own machine. Running an
independent program as a subprocess does not create a derivative work, which is
what keeps TruffleHog's AGPL-3.0 from reaching this codebase. See
docs/architecture/scanners.md.
